# Git hooks and shell scripts are executed by Git Bash, which cannot run a script
# whose shebang line ends in CR: `#!/bin/sh` resolves to a nonexistent
# interpreter and dies with "bad interpreter: No such file or directory".
#
# This matters most for .beads/hooks/*, which are version-controlled and run on
# every commit: with core.autocrlf=true a fresh clone would check them out with
# CRLF and they would fail OPEN -- exiting before doing anything, with nothing
# announcing that beads had stopped running.
*.sh            text eol=lf
*.py            text eol=lf
.beads/hooks/*  text eol=lf
